## Overview
Main agent runtime loop for processing tasks.

## Lifecycle
1. Initialize database
2. Connect to event hub
3. Loop:
   - Get queue
   - Claim task (emit task_claimed)
   - Execute with session logging
   - Complete/Release (emit task_completed)
   - Check for new work

## Implementation (src/code/agent.ts)
```typescript
async function agentMain(agentId: string) {
  const db = await rebuildState()
  const subscriber = new EventSubscriber()
  subscriber.connect(agentId)

  while (true) {
    const queue = getAgentQueue(db, agentId)
    const task = queue.find(t => !t.assigned_to)
    if (task) {
      emit({ type: 'task_claimed', actor: agentId, target: task.id })
      await executeTask(agentId, task)
      emit({ type: 'task_completed', ... })
    } else {
      await sleep(1000)
    }
  }
}
```

## Acceptance Criteria
- Reliable task processing
- Proper event lifecycle

## Overview
Event hub using Unix socket for real-time event distribution to agents.

## Implementation (src/code/hub.ts)

```typescript
class EventHub {
  private clients: Set<Socket> = new Set()

  start() {
    const server = createServer((client) => {
      this.clients.add(client)
      client.on('close', () => this.clients.delete(client))
    })
    server.listen('.kimmi/events.sock')
  }

  broadcast(event: Event) {
    const line = JSON.stringify(event) + '\n'
    for (const client of this.clients) {
      client.write(line)
    }
  }
}
```

## Protocol
- Newline-delimited JSON (same as events.jsonl)
- Pub/sub model

## Acceptance Criteria
- Real-time event distribution
- Multiple clients supported

## Overview
